ate address. Redirect hops are validated strictly whatever this says, and a public"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deployment that sets it has removed the control that makes "},{"code":"169.254.169.254","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unreachable."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy\/allowhttp"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"CimdPolicy","abstract":[{"text":"Whether, and on what terms, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"text":" that is a URL is resolved by fetching the document","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it names (T21.5, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"draft-ietf-oauth-client-id-metadata-document"},{"text":"). # Why this is one nested","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"policy rather than nine fields Every field here is a term of a single decision — ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"do we","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fetch a stranger’s URL and make a client out of what comes back","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — and none of them means","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anything without [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::enabled"},{"text":"]. A tenant that states a CIMD posture states all of it; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant that states none inherits its organization’s whole posture rather than half of one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is the only merge that cannot produce a combination neither party wrote. # The two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields that can widen, and the seven that cannot [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::enabled"},{"text":"] and [","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::allow_http"},{"type":"text","text":"]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": a tenant may turn either off but never on, exactly as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dynamic_registration"},{"type":"text","text":" may only move down its ladder. Everything else names "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"domains or "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this tenant’s","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" bounds, and there is no sense in which one tenant’s list of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trusted publishers is stricter than another’s — the same argument ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OidcPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":"] already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts"},{"type":"text","text":". # Every bound here is a security control"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::max_metadata_bytes"},{"type":"text","text":"], ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::min_cache_secs"},{"type":"text","text":"] and ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::max_cache_secs"},{"type":"text","text":"] are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tuning knobs. They are, respectively, the ceiling on a read from an attacker-chosen URL, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floor under how often that read may be repeated, and the ceiling on how long its result may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be trusted. Each is clamped again in code against the three constants above, so a settings"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row written by hand cannot lift them."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CimdPolicy"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","kind":"symbol","title":"AxiamSDK","abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/CimdPolicy/allowHttp":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Permit an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http:\/\/"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http:\/\/"},{"type":"text","text":" fetch. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Development only, and it does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more than its name says."}]},{"type":"text","text":" AXIAM’s shared SSRF guard couples the scheme rule to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"address rule — the same seam that lets an integration test point a fetch at a loopback"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mock server — so a tenant that allows "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http"},{"type":"text","text":" also allows the first hop to resolve to a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"private address. Redirect hops are validated strictly whatever this says, and a public","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deployment that sets it has removed the control that makes ","type":"text"},{"code":"169.254.169.254","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unreachable.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/CimdPolicy\/allowHttp","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/cimdpolicy\/allowhttp","role":"symbol"